        "id": 1085182
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T16:11:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would also prefer that but subscribing in suggestions service is not retriggering rendering as subscribing to @state in element. I would need to create a model for isGenereatedSuggestedFixEnabled and subscribe in element to it to be able to retrigger rendering.\n\nIf we agree I can do follow-up change with introducing suggestion-model that element can subscribe on.",
      "parentUuid": "8755ddd4_813aef06",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 638,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 639,
        "endChar": 34
      },
      "revId": "45e49c108594ab3b028b1db9cc0736f6c816cd42",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f62a15cb_7920a3cd",
        "filename": "polygerrit-ui/app/elements/checks/gr-checks-results.ts",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 639,
      "author": {
        "id": 1013302
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-18T17:18:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, that is a bit tricky. Feel free to submit as is and follow up.\n\nSuggestionsService could have a `suggestionsServiceUpdated$` observable that emits `true` each time `suggestionsProvider` or `change` are updated. Then `gr-checks-results.ts` could subscribe to that and call `requestUpdate()` on emission.\n\nThat would encapsulate `suggestionsProvider` or `change` inside the service, which I think would be worthwhile to do.\n\nAlternativly the service could create an observable that emits a utility function, and that function is then stored as @state. I am not yet sure whether I like the idea of observables emitting functions.",
      "parentUuid": "d0ae183a_25be5ce6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 638,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 639,
        "endChar": 34
